solution:
**Given:**

cos x - 3sin x = sqrt 3 sin x

**Calculation:**

Step 1: Move terms involving sin x to one side:

cos x = sqrt{3} sin x + 3 sin x

⇒ cos x = sin x (sqrt{3} + 3)

Step 2: Divide both sides by cos x:

dfrac{sin x}{cos x} = dfrac{1}{sqrt{3} + 3}

⇒ tan x = dfrac{1}{sqrt{3} + 3}

Step 3: Rationalize the denominator:

tan x = dfrac{1}{sqrt{3} + 3} times dfrac{sqrt{3} - 3}{sqrt{3} - 3} = dfrac{sqrt{3} - 3}{(sqrt{3})² - 9}

⇒ tan x = dfrac{sqrt{3} - 3}{3 - 9} = dfrac{sqrt{3} - 3}{-6}

**∴ The value of tan x = dfrac{3 - sqrt{3}}{6}**..
